<title>GREECE: BANK OF CYPRUS CUTS MORTGAGE RATE TO 13.9PCT.</title>
<headline>BANK OF CYPRUS CUTS MORTGAGE RATE TO 13.9PCT.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Cyprus which launched</p>
<p>innovative housing loans in foreign currency said it is cutting</p>
<p>its drachma mortgage rate down to 13.9 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;The Bank of Cyprus breaks the 14.0 percent barrier in</p>
<p>mortgage rates,&quot; it said on Monday.</p>
<p>Its loan rate structure had as follows:</p>
<p>** Base drachma lending rate at 15.5 percent</p>
<p>** Home improvement loan at 18.0 percent</p>
<p>** Mortgage rate at 13.9 percent</p>
<p>** Consumer loans at 19.75 percent</p>
<p>Bank of Cyprus deposit rates:</p>
<p>** CYPLUS account rate up to 10.75 percent</p>
<p>** Savings deposit rate at 9.5 percent</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
